From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Subject: kcm: link the Screensavers page from Power Management

Daniel Ramos, 2026-10-14 and 2026-11-24 (queue row 96): the screensavers have a
System Settings page of their own (sparky-stereo-screensavers: the list of
every screensaver, a small preview, a full-screen preview, the show's times),
and the pages a person looks on for it lead there: Display & Monitor, Power
Management, Screen Locking and Wallpaper. Power Management gets a button in its page's actions, in its header, and one in the
related pages of its advanced settings, beside Graphics.

The button opens kcm_sparkystereo_screensavers through KCMLauncher, so the
page opens inside System Settings; the patched package depends on
sparky-stereo-screensavers, so the button never leads nowhere.
The string carries no translation here: KDE forks take translations only from
KDE's translation teams, the edition's catalogues are in
sparky-os/translations/powerdevil-screensavers-link.po.patch.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2
---
diff --git a/kcm/ui/GlobalConfig.qml b/kcm/ui/GlobalConfig.qml
--- a/kcm/ui/GlobalConfig.qml
+++ b/kcm/ui/GlobalConfig.qml
@@ -374,6 +374,7 @@
                 desktopSessionsPage.implicitWidth,
                 activitiesPage.implicitWidth,
                 graphicsPage.implicitWidth,
+                screensaversPage.implicitWidth,
             )
 
             MostUsedItem {
@@ -430,6 +431,14 @@
                 Layout.preferredWidth: relatedPagesLayout.maxPageButtonImplicitWidth
                 onClicked: KCM.KCMLauncher.openSystemSettings("kcm_sparkystereo_graphics")
             }
+            MostUsedItem {
+                id: screensaversPage
+                kcmIcon: "preferences-desktop-screensaver"
+                kcmName: i18nc("@text:button Name of KCM", "Screensavers")
+                Accessible.name: i18n("Open \"Screensavers\" settings page")
+                Layout.preferredWidth: relatedPagesLayout.maxPageButtonImplicitWidth
+                onClicked: KCM.KCMLauncher.openSystemSettings("kcm_sparkystereo_screensavers")
+            }
         }
     }
 }
diff --git a/kcm/ui/main.qml b/kcm/ui/main.qml
--- a/kcm/ui/main.qml
+++ b/kcm/ui/main.qml
@@ -15,13 +15,20 @@
 
     KCM.ConfigModule.buttons: KCM.ConfigModule.Default | KCM.ConfigModule.Apply | KCM.ConfigModule.Help
 
-    actions: Kirigami.Action {
-        text: i18nc("@action:button", "Configure Advanced &Settings…")
-        icon.name: "settings-configure"
-        enabled: kcm.powerManagementServiceRegistered
-        displayHint: Kirigami.DisplayHint.KeepVisible
-        onTriggered: { kcm.push("GlobalConfig.qml"); }
-    }
+    actions: [
+        Kirigami.Action {
+            text: i18nc("@action:button", "Configure Advanced &Settings…")
+            icon.name: "settings-configure"
+            enabled: kcm.powerManagementServiceRegistered
+            displayHint: Kirigami.DisplayHint.KeepVisible
+            onTriggered: { kcm.push("GlobalConfig.qml"); }
+        },
+        Kirigami.Action {
+            text: i18nc("@action:button opens the Screensavers settings page", "Screensavers…")
+            icon.name: "preferences-desktop-screensaver"
+            onTriggered: KCM.KCMLauncher.openSystemSettings("kcm_sparkystereo_screensavers")
+        }
+    ]
 
     implicitWidth: Kirigami.Units.gridUnit * 30
     implicitHeight: Kirigami.Units.gridUnit * 35
